Docker is a platform used to build, run, and manage applications.
It packages an application with all its dependencies into a container.
A Docker image is a template used to create containers.
A Docker container is a running instance of an image.
Dockerfile contains instructions to build a Docker image.
docker build creates an image from a Dockerfile.
docker run creates and starts a container.
Docker Hub is a public registry for storing and sharing images.
Amazon ECR is AWS's private container registry for Docker images.
Docker makes applications portable, consistent, and easy to deploy
